h\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja \\\n```\n*   **`-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"`:** Specifies the **source directory**. This is where the downloaded git repository resides.\n*   **`-B \"${srcdir}/build\"`:** Specifies the **build directory**. CMake will generate all intermediate files (object files, makefiles) here, keeping the source tree clean.\n*   **`-G Ninja`:** Sets the build system generator to **Ninja**. Ninja is significantly faster than Make for large C++ projects like `llama.cpp`.\n\n### 4"}